Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:03:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 075/342] tcp: _Spawn() resets local address
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* That means if _Bind() fails (or the socket is dropped before), the
  EndpointManager will not assume this endpoint has been added to the
  connection hash yet.
* Otherwise, Unbind() would then have tried to remove it from the
  connection hash which led to a panic.

Change-Id: Id7ab18174fd9874fef5e7c5aa6a9f9328c1b89ca
Reviewed-on: https://review.haiku-os.org/c/haiku/+/12744
Reviewed-by: Axel Dörfler <axeld@pinc-software.de>
Tested-by: Commit checker robot <no-reply+buildbot@haiku-os.org>
Haiku-Format: Haiku-format Bot <no-reply+haikuformatbot@haiku-os.org>
Reviewed-by: waddlesplash <waddlesplash@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit ad3afc3a2f1b4b10a3e918dec40d9b4d78f303e3)

Fork: fixes the "bound endpoint ... not in hash!" panic when sshd closed
its listening socket at shutdown on a C2 (a SYN that came in while
DHCP was still configuring the interface left a child that failed to bind).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp
index b82fb00535..8cd1fa0b58 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 /*
